                New Alpha-Based Personal Workstations
                   Boost Digital's Windows NT Lead


... Shipment of 50,000th NT Personal Workstation Marks Digital as 
              Front-runner in Explosive New Market ...


MAYNARD, Mass., January 8, 1997 -- Digital Equipment Corporation, 
the world's leading supplier of Windows NT personal workstations, 
today announced two new models based on the company's fastest 64-
bit Alpha microprocessors.  DIGITAL's new Personal Workstation 500a 
and 433a deliver breakthrough levels of Windows NT Workstation 
performance, the world's fastest Windows NT 3D graphics, and 
excellent prices for designers, animators, engineers and other 
technical professionals.

     While vendors such as Compaq and HP are just shipping their 
first-ever personal workstations, DIGITAL is rounding out its second 
generation of Intel- and Alpha-based Windows NT personal 
workstations.  Underscoring DIGITAL's leadership position, the 
company also announced today that it has shipped its 50,000th 
personal workstation to United Space Alliance, a joint venture of 
Lockheed Martin and Boeing.

     "There is a simple reason why DIGITAL is number one in Windows 
NT personal workstations: ours are the fastest Windows NT 
workstations in the world, they cost far less than what customers 
are used to paying, and they run the most popular workstation 
applications," said Philippe Ribeyre, vice president of the DIGITAL 
Workstation Business Segment. "And no one can touch DIGITAL's 
PowerStorm 3D graphics performance.  Meanwhile, HP and Compaq are 
just getting started, delivering basic personal workstation 
products with no graphics or processor head room." 

Delivering Windows NT Workstation Solutions to Technical Users

     The DIGITAL Personal Workstation 433a and the DIGITAL Personal 
Workstation 500a are designed for customers in the EDA, MCAD, 
digital content creation, GIS, scientific, and software development 
markets. The systems provide a distinct competitive advantage to 
these customers through their combination of unparalleled 
workstation performance, dramatically lower costs and Windows NT 
ease of use.

     The new DIGITAL Personal Workstations are a key part of  
DIGITAL's continuing strategy of dominating the market for Windows 
NT solutions across corporate and technical computing environments. 
The DIGITAL Personal Workstations support thousands of top Windows 
NT workstation applications, including PTC Pro-E, Softimage 3D, 
Solidworks 95, and -- through FX!32 -- mainstream productivity 
tools, such as Microsoft Office '95 and Adobe Photoshop.  Each model 
ships with Windows NT Workstation version 4.0 and FX!32 factory-
installed.

     "The introduction of Microsoft Windows NT Workstation 4.0 has 
accelerated the shift away from high priced proprietary UNIX 
workstations," said Jim Allchin, Senior Vice President of the 
Personal and Business Systems Group at Microsoft Corporation.   
"Microsoft and DIGITAL are working together to address the needs of 
workstation customers who want industry standards-based solutions 
that offer superior price/performance, the widest array of software 
and the lowest total cost of ownership."

Benchmarks Beat HP, Sun, SGI

     Assisted by the DIGITAL-designed Pyxis chipset, which 
implements a high-bandwidth, low-latency 128-bit memory bus, the 
DIGITAL Personal Workstation 500a tore through the Texas Instruments 
Pro/Engineer benchmark at a phenomenal 56 minutes; the DIGITAL 
Personal Workstation 433a clocked in at 61 minutes.  These results, 
where a lower score means better performance, topped those of the 
SGI Indigo2 R10000 Solid IMPACT (79 minutes), Intergraph TDZ310/Z13 
(106 minutes), HP B160L (111 minutes), and Sun Ultra 2/1200 (108 
minutes).  Even more significant, the 500a and 433a are available 
for a fraction of the cost of the UNIX workstations they 
outperformed.

     With Alpha's superior floating-point performance capabilities, 
the DIGITAL Personal Workstation 500a and 433a also deliver the 
fastest Windows NT Workstation 3D graphics solution available among 
all personal workstations. Running the CDRS-03 benchmark, where a 
higher score means better performance, the PowerStorm 4DT graphics 
achieved a mark of 41.63 for the 433a, and 45 (est.) for the 500a. 
This world-class performance compares with drastically slower scores 
for the SGI 02 R10000 (13.57), as well as the higher priced SGI High 
IMPACT (32.09).

     "Finally, you can get a screaming Alpha all decked out for 
multimedia," said Jerry Flynn, Technical Specialist, Bentley 
Systems, Inc.  "It does not get any better - this baby smokes."

RISC/CISC Capabilities Protect Customers' Investments

     Through DIGITAL'S PowerGrade processor upgrade feature, DIGITAL 
Personal Workstation customers are given the option of do-it-
yourself upgrades to more powerful Intel or 64-bit Alpha processors 
as they become available.  This unique CISC-to-RISC capability 
ensures investment protection by eliminating costly hardware 
upgrades, giving customers the opportunity to tailor a personal 
workstation solution to fit their specific Windows NT needs.

Configuration and Pricing

     The DIGITAL Personal Workstation 500a and 433a support from 32 
to 384 MB of synchronous DRAM with ECC support. Standard 
configurations feature an Ultrawide SCSI disk controller, 2.1 GB 
hard drive, 8X EIDE CD-ROM drive, integrated 10BaseT/10Base2 
Ethernet, and integrated 16-bit audio.

     Graphics options include DIGITAL's high-performance PowerStorm 
3D graphics, Matrox Millennium and AccelGraphics AccelPro Series.

     Prices for the DIGITAL Personal Workstation 433a start at 
US$4,995 with 64 MB of RAM and Matrox graphics. The DIGITAL Personal 
Workstation 500a with 64 MB of RAM and AccelPro 2500 graphics is 
priced under US$10,000.  The systems are available immediately from 
DIGITAL's channel partners. 

50,000 Personal Workstations and Counting...

     A major procurement by United Space Alliance has catapulted 
shipments of the DIGITAL Personal Workstations over the 50,000-unit 
mark -- cementing DIGITAL's leadership position in this market. 

     DIGITAL has sold more Windows NT personal workstations than any 
other vendor, and continues to increase the range of personal 
workstation products available to its customers.

     "We reviewed Windows NT workstations from several different 
vendors to run our design automation software," said Jim Melton, of  
United Space Alliance System Design and Analysis. "Our choice was 
based on the performance and price of DIGITAL's personal 
workstations and the strength of DIGITAL's service and support. 
DIGITAL has been in the workstation market for more than a decade, 
and the experience shows." 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems.  DIGITAL's scalable Alpha and Intel platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 

     For more information on the DIGITAL Personal Workstations, see 
http://www.workstation.digital.com

