                  Digital Leads Market with New MMX
                     Technology-Based Solutions

     Among the First to Ship Mobile and Desktop Clients Based on
   New Intel Processors; HiNote VP 500 Series with MMX Technology
          Breaks Performance Record for Notebook Computing

MAYNARD, Mass., Jan. 8, 1997 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
reinforced its leadership in the enterprise computing market today 
with new personal computers based on the Pentium processor with MMX 
technology announced today by Intel Corporation.  Joining the 
company's popular line of competitively priced mobile and desktop 
client solutions designed for the Windows-based enterprise are new
models of the Digital HiNote VP 500 series notebooks -- 
incorporating 150- and 166-megahertz (MHz) versions of the new 
processor -- and a 200MHz model of the Celebris FX desktop computer.

     Digital is among the first in the industry to ship products 
based on Intel's new processors and the new HiNote VP 500 series 
notebooks with MMX technology deliver unprecedented performance.  
The company believes the new notebooks are the first to achieve 
overall scores as high as 100 on the industry-standard "WinStone 32" 
performance benchmark test and as high as 80 on the "Winstone 96" 
test.

     "Digital continues to offer the commercial PC market the latest 
in enterprise solutions based on customer requirements," said Howard 
Elias, vice president of worldwide business segments in Digital's 
Personal Computer Business Unit. "Today's announcement reinforces 
yet again our leadership in delivering new products that lead the 
market in terms of features, performance, quality and value.  
Intel's Pentium processors with MMX technology enable a new level 
of multimedia and communications performance that will play an 
important and expanding role in Digital's product offerings this 
year."

Unprecedented Price/Performance in a Value-Line Notebook

     Digital's HiNote VP 500 series notebooks are leading the value 
segment in terms of price and performance for mobile client 
solutions. Industry-standard benchmark tests have demonstrated the 
HiNote VP 500's superior performance against high-end notebooks from 
competitors including Compaq, Toshiba and IBM.  Available 
immediately worldwide, the new HiNote VP model 545 is based on the 
150MHz version of Intel's new Pentium processor with MMX technology, 
and furthers Digital's competitive edge by providing continued 
industry-leading performance and high-end features at less than 
$4,000 (estimated U.S. street price).  The company will ship the 
166MHz version of the HiNote VP 500 later this quarter.

     Optimized for maximum performance, the HiNote VP 500 series 
notebooks with MMX technology maintain the HiNote VP 500's top-ranked 
competitive position for performance leadership in mobile client computing.
The new 150 and 166MHz models with Intel's MMX technology shattered the 
performance barrier on the "WinStone 32" and "WinStone 96" benchmark 
tests with scores averaging 54 to 66 percent faster overall performance 
than Compaq's LTE 5300 or Toshiba's Tecra 720CDT, and 23 to 33 percent 
faster than IBM's high-end ThinkPad 760ED. The HiNote VP model 535 -- 
announced last September and based on the 133MHz version of Intel's 
standard Pentium processor technology -- was the previous leader in 
overall "WinStone 96" performance, with scores ranking more than 40 
percent faster than the Compaq and Toshiba systems and 16 percent faster 
than IBM's solution.

     Combining the exceptional video and graphics capabilities of 
the HiNote VP 500 series notebooks with Intel's new MMX technology 
also brings a new dimension of multimedia power and performance to 
the value notebook space. With support for full-screen, full-motion 
MPEG (Motion Pictures Expert Group) video running at 30-frames-per-
second, the HiNote VP 500 series notebooks with MMX technology 
provide faster, smoother video that brings multimedia presentations 
to life.  The new processor from Intel provides up to 20 percent 
faster performance running existing software applications, and as 
much as 60 percent faster multimedia performance when used with new 
MMX-enabled applications.

     Digital's HiNote VP 500 series notebooks with MMX technology 
also deliver long battery life. Through the use of Smart battery 
technology in conjunction with "Advanced Metal" Enhanced Nickel 
Metal Hydride and Lithium-Ion batteries, the HiNote VP 500 series 
delivers up to 10 hours of high-performance mobile computing using 
the system's dual-battery option.

     Other leading-edge notebook features include 12.1-inch SVGA 
(Super Video Graphics Array) active-matrix color displays, 128-bit 
graphics acceleration with MPEG support and a removable, internal 
6X-speed CD-ROM drive in the system's modular expansion bay. The 
modular expansion bay also supports a removable diskette drive or an 
optional second battery, which are interchangeable with the system's 
CD-ROM drive.  The HiNote VP 500 series scales from 8-megabytes (MB) 
of Extended Data Out (EDO) memory up to 40MB and includes removable 
hard drives supporting up to 1.44-gigabytes (GB) of storage 
capacity.

     The new HiNote VP 500 series notebooks with MMX technology come 
pre-loaded with Windows 95 or Windows for Workgroups 3.11 and are 
fully enabled for mobile computing under Windows NT using the 
company's Windows NT 4.0 driver kit.  Developed exclusively by 
Digital and optimized for Windows NT Workstation, the driver kit 
provides enhanced power management and plug-and-play-like 
functionality -- making Windows NT-based notebook computing 
practical for mobile professionals.

Unparalleled Power and Performance for the Enterprise Desktop

     Enterprise customers require PC designs with long life, 
expandability and the capability to take advantage of new 
applications being developed today. Digital's Celebris family is a 
premium line of "enterprise-ready" clients that make it easier to 
install, configure and manage desktops within the enterprise. By 
incorporating Intel's latest Pentium processor with MMX technology, 
the new Celebris FX model 5200M provides the leading-edge technology 
and investment protection of key importance to enterprise customers.

     With up to 15 percent faster overall Pentium performance and as 
much as 60 percent faster performance on selected MMX-enabled 
applications, the new Celebris FX 5200M brings a broad range of 
power and performance options to the enterprise desktop environment.  
Based on the 200MHz version of the new Pentium processor with MMX 
technology, the Celebris FX 5200M includes 32MB of EDO memory, a 
2.1GB EIDE (Enhanced Integrated Drive Electronics) hard drive and an 
8X-speed CD-ROM drive.  The system is available immediately in the 
United States and Europe with an estimated street price starting at 
U.S. $2,589, and will ship in Japan at the end of February.

"Get Connected" to the Enterprise

     The Digital HiNote VP 500 series notebooks and Celebris FX 
desktops are ideal solutions for customers who need the most 
performance for the money in enterprise-ready mobile and desktop 
client solutions.  The network-ready clients are designed to keep 
users connected to the enterprise with pre-loaded Digital 
ClientWORKS network management software, DMI support and expansion 
options that include built-in network connectivity.

     Digital's solutions are the leading choice for customers 
deploying Windows-based computing across the enterprise. The company 
offers enterprise customers superior value with client/server 
solutions optimized for Windows and Windows NT environments, global 
services and support, and solutions delivered through alliances with 
industry leaders.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha and Intel platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
