          Aggressive Digital Pricing Dramatically Increases
                Affordability of Alpha Computer Line

              ...Workstation and Server Prices Reduced
              Up To 42 and 47 Percent, Respectively...

       ...New Server Configurations Quadruple Memory Capacity
                         at Minimal Cost...

MAYNARD, Mass., January 9, 1997 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today reduced prices by as much as 47 percent on its industry- 
leading 64-bit AlphaServer systems, 42 percent on its powerful 
AlphaStation workstations, and 55 percent on memory options. The 
pricing reflects intensified competitive positioning for DIGITAL's 
workstation products, and volume manufacturing and lower-priced 
memory for its AlphaServer line.

     DIGITAL also introduced new base-level server configurations 
that provide as much as four times the memory of current systems at 
little or no extra cost.

     "Today's aggressive price reductions and new base-level system 
configurations enable even more customers in a broader range of 
markets to leverage the breakthrough performance and price/
performance advantages of the Alpha platform," said Harry Copperman, 
vice president and general manager, Systems Business Unit.  "They 
will benefit from the power of complete 64-bit solutions that 
include very-large-memory (VLM) capability, exceptional scalability, 
and protection from costly migration."

Pricing highlights include:

     *	Midrange AlphaServer 4000 5/300 system (used for line-of-
     	business, Internet/intranet, LAN, and departmental 
        applications) now priced at $31,500 with 512 MB of memory, 
     	a 47 percent savings.  System has capacity for two 300 MHz 
        Alpha processors and up to 4 GB of 64-bit VLM64.  Similar 
        savings now available on the higher-capacity AlphaServer 
        4000 5/400 and 4100 systems.

     *	AlphaServer 8200 5/440 system reduced 20 percent to $224,400 
        with 2 GB memory. Similarly, flagship AlphaServer 8400 5/440 
        system is now $344,400 with 2 GB memory, a 14 percent 
        reduction.

     *	Pricing for low-end AlphaServer 1000A 5/333 with 256 MB 
        memory reduced 12 percent to $13,945.

     *	DIGITAL memory now available for as little as $19/megabyte, 
        making it among the most aggressively priced memory in the 
        industry. AlphaServer systems are now configured with up to 
        four times previous memory at little or no increase in 
        price.

     *	AlphaStation 600/333, with DIGITAL UNIX, 128 MB memory, 2 GB 
        disk, 21-inch monitor, and PowerStorm 4D40T graphics, priced 
        at $24,995, a savings of 42 percent.

     *	AlphaStation 500/500, the world's fastest desktop 
        workstation, with DIGITAL UNIX, 128 MB memory, 2 GB disk, 
        21-inch monitor, and PowerStorm 4D40T graphics, reduced 20 
        percent to $39,995.

     *	AlphaStation 500/333, with DIGITAL UNIX, 128 MB memory, 2 GB 
        disk, 21-inch monitor, and PowerStorm 4D40T graphics, now 
        priced 20 percent lower at $21,995. 

     *	Entry-level AlphaStation 255/300 workstation, with DIGITAL 
        UNIX, 64 MB memory, 1 GB disk, 17-inch monitor, and entry-
     	level graphics, now priced at $9,995, a savings of 28 
        percent. 

     Server pricing changes are effective worldwide; workstation 
pricing in U.S. and Europe.

Larger Memory Systems

     "Lower memory prices are fueling the trend toward larger-memory 
systems," said Pauline Nist, vice president of DIGITAL's AlphaServer 
Business Segment. "Customers are becoming aware of the dramatic 
performance and scaling gains when larger portions of database-
intensive applications are accessed directly from memory. 
Very-Large-Memory AlphaServer systems, combined with 64-bit 
addressing and raw speed, give customers a superior, high-
performance computing platform."

     The new prices make the AlphaServer 4100 systems -- the first 
midrange systems to offer VLM -- 34 percent more affordable than a 
comparable Sun UltraEnterprise 4000 system. The AlphaServer 1000A 
system is now priced to compete head-on with the Compaq 1500. And 
DIGITAL's high-quality memory is now price-competitive with any 
other memory in the industry.

Desktop Visual Computing Excellence

     "Reducing AlphaStation prices is a key element of DIGITAL's 
continued drive to provide desktop visual computing excellence to 
our customers," said Philippe Ribeyre, vice president of DIGITAL's 
Workstation Business Segment.  "Today, we deliver the world's 
fastest UNIX and Windows NT 3D workstations at a fraction of 
competitors' prices."

     As a result of the pricing reductions, an AlphaStation 500/333 
delivers up to 21 percent more performance at 21 percent less cost 
than an HP C160L-Vis24, and up to 20 percent better performance than 
a comparably priced Sun UltraSPARC 170E.

     AlphaServer systems and AlphaStation workstations are based on 
the powerful, reliable, and affordable 64-bit Alpha RISC 
architecture.  DIGITAL provides its customers all the benefits of 
the company's strategic partnerships with leading software vendors, 
and a clear path to the future without costly and time-consuming 
migrations. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
server solutions, from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems.  DIGITAL's scalable Alpha and Intel platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 

     For more information visit the following Digital Web sites: 
www.digital.com/info/alphaserver, www.workstation.digital.com
