             Digital Announces Industry's Most Complete
        Storage Management Solutions for Microsoft Windows NT


MAYNARD, Mass., January 20, 1997 -- Digital Equipment Corporation
today expanded its leading portfolio of Windows NT solutions across 
the enterprise with new and enhanced storage management solutions. 
These enable customers to manage, store, protect, and backup their 
data in distributed Windows NT environments.

Today's introduction includes: 

     o 	An enhanced version of Networker Save and Restore for 
        Windows NT -- the most complete storage management software 
        for Windows NT environments;

     o 	The world's most scalable digital linear tape (DLT) drive, 
        and enhanced automated DLT library support;

     o 	The world's fastest 4mm digital audio tape (DAT) and 
        autoloader; and

     o 	A new 12X CD-ROM, three times faster than previous versions.
     

     "As more and more customers commit their mission-critical
applications and data to the Windows NT environment, departmental 
backup solutions are becoming increasingly important," said Dave 
Coombs, vice president of Worldwide Storage Marketing for Digital.  

"The new StorageWorks backup products represent the most 
sophisticated storage management software on the market and the 
highest capacity backup devices. They offer significant productivity 
gains to customers who use the Windows NT operating system." 

Enterprise-Wide Storage Management for Windows NT

     Networker Save and Restore for Windows NT, Digital's leadership
network storage management application, includes new features that 
offer users greater choices for backing up and protecting widely 
dispersed data throughout an enterprise. It is the only networked 
storage management software that scales to 500 clients in a Windows 
NT environment. 

     The software, which supports Digital's StorageWorks tapes,
autoloaders, and libraries, enables customers to manage multiple DLT
libraries as a single unit. They can manage up to five DLT libraries
for a total of 52.8 TB of backup storage. 

     In addition, Networker Save and Restore for Windows NT software 
is designed for use with Microsoft's BackOffice suite of software 
products.  The server edition supports Windows NT version 4.0. 
Digital is also announcing a new NetWorker Archive module that 
delivers advanced file-level archiving to off-load long-term 
storage. 

     "Networker Save and Restore is a total storage management 
solution, allowing customers to manage most of the systems and 
devices in their enterprise -- from PCs with single tape drives to 
multi-server networks with multiple tape libraries," added Coombs. 
"The software offers more performance and functionality than most 
Windows NT-based backup utilities that are unable to protect 
critical data on remote systems." 

New Digital Linear Tape Drive and Multiple Library Support

     Because DLT is recognized as the most cost-effective backup 
technology in the industry, Digital is expanding its offerings with 
a new DLT drive and support for multiple DLT libraries.

     The DLT drive can store up to 70 GB of information per
cartridge, 75 percent more than the previous drive could handle.
Native transfer rates of up to 5 MB per second or 18 GB per hour 
meet or exceed the requirements of most high-end workstations, 
network servers, and departmental or workgroup systems. 

     "With the new DLT drive, some customers will be able to back up 
a week's worth of information on a single cartridge, and back it up 
faster than ever before," said Coombs. "The drive lowers the cost of 
both attended and unattended backup and addresses customers' needs 
to back up an increasing amount of data in a constantly shrinking 
window of time." 

     In addition, Digital's DLT Tape Libraries are available with
software that enables up to five libraries to act as a single unit. 
These automated libraries, with appropriate software such as 
Networker Save and Restore, can access up to 52.8 TB of storage 
backup. 

     Multiple DLT libraries, which can store high volumes of data at 
a low cost per MB and without human error, are ideal for 
Hierarchical Storage Management (HSM), imaging, multimedia, 
archiving, near- and on-line storage, and unattended backup 
applications. 

Industry's Fastest 4 mm Digital Audio Tape Drives and Autoloaders

     Because many customers with small- to medium-sized computing
environments have more data to back up than ever and are on tight 
budgets, Digital is offering a new 4 mm low-cost DAT drive and 
autoloader. With transfer rates of up to 775 KB per second native 
and up to 1,550 KB per second compressed, the new drive and 
autoloader are the fastest in the industry and provide twice the 
performance of competitors' products.

     The DAT drive is especially designed for file, print, and 
application servers, workstations, and data centers. It provides 4 
GB native capacity and 8 GB compressed capacity and is available in 
tabletop and StorageWorks system building block configurations. 

     The new autoloader is designed for unattended backup and 
archiving applications. It provides up to 64 GB of capacity, 
supporting up to eight cartridges in a single magazine and enables 
backups of up to 8 GB of storage in less than 1.5 hours.

New CD-ROM for Demanding Video Applications       

     CD-ROMs, because of their large capacity, are becoming popular 
for applications such as training, games, online reference 
libraries, and multimedia applications that depend on graphics, 
animation, sound, and full motion video, especially in Internet 
environments. Digital's new CD-ROM drastically improves the 
performance loading of applications and video playback of multimedia 
applications, eliminating dropped segments and jittery video. It 
provides extremely fast transfer rates of 12X with 1,800 KB per 
second throughput and is three times faster than the previous model. 

Pricing and Availability

     The price for Networker Save and Restore for Windows NT server
edition is $995; the network edition with 10 client connections is 
$2,750. The DLT drive is $11,995 list. The software that enables the
connection of up to five of Digital's tape libraries is included 
with the libraries. The DAT drive starts at $1,900. Prices for the 
DAT tape autoloader start at $3,650. The 12X CD-ROM is $490. 

     The DLT drive will be available in March. The 12X CD-ROM will 
be available in February.  The other products are available 
immediately. The products are available from Digital and its 
channels partners.

     For more information about Digital's complete line of storage 
hardware and software products, call 1-800-STORWORK (1-800-786-7967) 
or visit http://www.storage.digital.com on the World Wide Web. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems.  Digital's scalable Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
