              Digital Extends Benefits of IP Switching
                       to Major New Market


 ...Helps businesses with packet-based networks improve performance, 
       simplify operations, and reduce costs over traditional
                         routed networks...

       ...Implementation is a free upgrade to industry-leading
                      GIGAswitch/FDDI System...

MAYNARD, Mass., January 20, 1997 -- Digital Equipment Corporation, 
already a leader in delivering networking solutions optimized for 
the Internet Protocol (IP), today became the first vendor to offer 
the performance,  cost of ownership, and management advantages of IP 
switching to businesses with packet technology at the heart of their 
campus backbone networks.  Called IP packet switching, the solution 
comprises new software that adds features to DIGITAL's award- 
winning GIGAswitch/FDDI System, giving customers substantial 
improvements over traditional routed networks.  IP packet switching 
complements DIGITAL's GIGAswitch/IP Solution, which is based on 
protocols that Ipsilon Networks developed for cell-based 
Asynchronous Transfer Mode (ATM) networks.

     Today's announcement also includes new ATM and Fast Ethernet 
line cards that enable the GIGAswitch/FDDI to support multiple 
technologies; a new GIGAswitch/FDDI package that gives businesses a 
very low cost of entry to this powerful solution; and price 
reductions up to 30% on popular GIGAswitch/FDDI line cards that give 
customers an easy, economical way to meet increasing network needs. 
 
     "Customers have been very enthusiastic about the advantages of 
IP switching on ATM networks, and those not yet ready to move to ATM 
want the same capabilities on their packet networks,"  said Robert 
J. Rennick, vice president and general manager of DIGITAL's Network 
Product Business.  "As the market leader in providing well-proven, 
high-performance FDDI networks for example, the GIGAswitch/FDDI 
already carries most of the packets transferred today on the World 
Wide Web as well as a high percentage of the packets transferred 
within bet-your-business enterprise networks -- DIGITAL is a natural 
to be first with IP packet switching. Our commitment to protecting 
customers' investments makes the free upgrade to the GIGAswitch/FDDI 
System the logical first step in deploying this key technology which 
improves the performance and extends the life of FDDI networks." 

IP Packet Switching Eliminates Need for Routers Between Subnets

     As customers address business needs by adding new users and new 
applications to their networks, they find themselves dividing their 
local area networks into smaller segments, or subnets, to make 
better use of their resources.  To communicate between the subnets 
network managers have added routers, but these routers, with their 
inherent latency and throughput limitations, have become network 
bottlenecks.   

     IP packet switching gives customers a more cost-effective, 
higher performance solution than traditional routing by enabling 
them to switch between and among the subnets. It also provides the 
broadcast limiting capability of routing, but without routing's 
management complexity and operational costs.  Routers can then be 
used where they are truly needed -- for wide area network (WAN) 
access and firewall security.

     IP packet switching delivers its advanced capabilities as a 
simple firmware upgrade to the GIGAswitch/FDDI System. It uses 
software to map an IP address to a Media Access Control (MAC) 
address and handles per-packet forwarding in hardware. Customers can 
deploy the new technology at their own pace, adding it when and 
where it makes the most sense.  They can also use it in a 
multivendor environment, because the GIGAswitch/FDDI enables 
end-to-end switching across any vendors' switches connected to the 
GIGAswitch/FDDI.

     "It's good to see a vendor delivering IP switching technology 
today targeted specifically at the corporate environment," said Eric 
Hindin, program manager at the Yankee Group.  "Combined with 
DIGITAL's existing hubs, switches, and routers, users can get a 
single vendor solution without having to face the forklift 
upgrades."
     
Phased Rollout of IP Switching Solves Today's Problems with 
Eye to the Future

     Part of the company's enVISN (enterprise Virtual Intelligent 
Switched Networks) architecture, DIGITAL's IP switching technology 
is rolling out in phases that enable customers to realize the 
business benefits of high performance networks today with a growth 
path to meet future requirements. 

     In Phase I, announced in July, DIGITAL introduced the 
GIGAswitch/IP Solution for ATM networks. Shipping since August, this 
first implementation uses the protocols developed by Ipsilon 
Networks and takes advantage of high performance circuit switching 
inherent in ATM networks. 

     Phase II, introduced today and rolling out over the coming 
months, provides IP packet switching software for the 
GIGAswitch/FDDI System, including connections to ATM and Fast 
Ethernet.  A new ATM line card (described below) provides an IP 
switch gateway capability to allow customers to enjoy the benefits 
of IP switching in a campus network that includes both ATM and 
packet- based switches.  A new Fast Ethernet line card (described 
below) extends IP packet switching to the Fast Ethernet environment 
from the GIGAswitch/FDDI system.

     Phase III will further integrate IP switching across mixed cell 
and packet networks by capitalizing on the attributes of  IPv6 .   
This solution will help customers migrate easily to evolving IPv6 
implementations. 

     "We have bet our business on DIGITAL's GIGAswitch/FDDI product, 
and it has never let me down," said Eric Landwehr, second Vice 
President at Sanford Bernstein in New York. "DIGITAL's IP packet 
switching technology is ideal for my network because it enables me 
to remove any existing router bottlenecks and it improves the 
overall performance of my network."

ATM Line Card Provides End-to-End Connectivity

     Also unveiled today is a new ATM line card that provides 
communication between FDDI and ATM end stations.  With its modular 
design, the line card fits into the GIGAswitch/ATM or 
GIGAswitch/FDDI Systems to provide seamless connectivity from both 
cells to packets and from end-station to end-station across the 
network.  The line card complies with ATM Forum standards and can 
act as an IP switching gateway to solutions based on Ipsilon's 
protocols.

New Line Card Brings Multi-Technology Support to GIGAswitch/FDDI 
System

     Announced today, the four-port Fast Ethernet line card enables 
businesses deploying Fast Ethernet solutions to connect them 
directly to the GIGAswitch/FDDI System to provide high-speed server 
and workgroup connectivity to the FDDI backbone. The total solution 
makes it easier for customers to manage FDDI, Fast Ethernet, and ATM 
technologies -- all in a single, proven system.

Product Pricing and Availability

     IP packet switching is available to existing GIGAswitch/FDDI 
customers as a free firmware upgrade.  The Version 3.2 upgrade kit 
will be available on the Web in March.  GIGAswitch/FDDI systems that 
ship in March will include the upgraded firmware.

     A new start-up package is available immediately for customers 
looking for a low cost of entry into this market. The two-port 
GIGAswitch/FDDI package with a two-port FDDI line card is priced at 
$24,400.  Prices for existing two- and four-port line cards are 
reduced from 25 - 30%, making it even more cost-effective for 
customers to add new capacity.

     The new four-port Fast Ethernet line card and new ATM line card 
will be available in September. 

     Additional information on DIGITAL's Network Product Business is 
available on the World Wide Web at http://www.networks.digital.com.

