              Digital Delivers Unique Desktop Services
                  for Enterprise Knowledge Workers


   ...Finally a Support Package that Focuses on Users' Information
             Needs, as well as Hardware and Software...


MAYNARD, Mass., Jan. 21, 1997 -- Digital Equipment Corporation today 
announced Client Support Service, a set of unique service plans that 
combine hardware support, software support, and personalized 
information services to meet the user's complete information-related 
needs.  

     Information services are initially provided in partnership with 
Individual, Inc., which delivers daily personalized intelligence 
reports culled from 700 news sources.  Digital plans to partner with 
other information sources in the near future.  The new comprehensive 
service further demonstrates Digital's commitment to becoming a 
leading provider of enterprise-wide desktop service and support. 

     "The effectiveness of today's knowledge workers is increasingly 
dependent upon the availability of the IT tools they use and their 
ability to obtain the most relevant information from a sea of data," 
said Digital's Vice President of Multivendor Desktop Services, Matt 
Kochan.  

     "Digital's Client Support Service supports knowledge workers' 
technology-enabled work style while addressing their ongoing 
personal information needs.  The comprehensive service plans ensure 
these workers have reliable access to the tools they need to 
maximize their productivity and responsiveness in today's 
competitive business environment," Kochan added.

     "Digital is providing a valuable service for knowledge 
workers," said Individual, Inc.'s Vice President of Marketing, 
Richard Vancil.  "The new service will save Digital customers 
countless hours of searching and reviewing irrelevant information.  
We are pleased to be part of an innovative approach that is sure to 
help organizations maintain a competitive edge."    

     Digital's Client Support Service is intended for enterprise 
knowledge workers using PCs or notebooks -- 75 percent of today's 
workforce.  Vital to the success of today's dynamic enterprise, 
these workers make key business decisions based on readily available 
information.  They work in environments with limited resources, a 
proliferation of information, and fast-paced technological 
advancements.

     Specific service plans are available to meet the support needs 
of the four types of clients typically found in today's business 
environment -- Enterprise, Knowledge, Mobile, and Power Clients. 
These plans are unique because they focus on the needs of these 
users, not just on the devices employed.

     Information-related services include NewsPage--a personalized 
news service provided daily via e-mail and web-based delivery by 
Individual Inc., and access to Electronic Bulletin Boards.  
Individual, Inc. delivers summarized information daily to the user's 
desktop from numerous sources, according to user-defined search/
retrieval guidelines.  The company provides pertinent, concise data 
about competitors, industries, products, customers, and more.

     Digital's Client Support Service can be purchased from Digital 
and its business partners at a monthly fixed price per user, 
enabling customers to easily forecast and budget the expense.  
Per-client monthly prices start at $29 for Enterprise Clients. The 
new packages complement but do not replace Digital's product-focused 
PC Utility life-cycle management service.  Business partners can use 
the service as a basis for crafting a full life-cycle solution of 
their own, similar to Digital's PC Utility offer. 

     The packages are available now in the U.S. and Canada.  They 
support the leading brands of PC hardware, peripherals, and desktop 
applications. 

     Headquartered in Burlington, Mass., Individual, Inc. is a 
pioneer and leading provider of personalized business news services.  
Its exclusive information retrieval and filtering technologies bring 
highly relevant news and information to more than 425,000 readers 
worldwide.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
server solutions from personal computers to integrated worldwide 
information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha and Intel platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
