                 AltaVista Search Network to Expand
             with Mirror Site for Asian Internet Users


         ...Malaysia Site to Become Third Affiliate in the
                   AltaVista Worldwide Network...


KUALA LUMPUR, Malaysia, and MAYNARD, Mass., January 29, 1997 -- 
Digital Equipment Corporation's AltaVista Internet Software 
subsidiary today announced the next phase of expansion in its 
AltaVista Worldwide Network with the signing of a Network Affiliate 
agreement with a Malaysian company to establish an AltaVista 
Internet Search mirror site in Asia.  Alam Teknokrat Sdn Bhd, a 
Malaysia Internet Content Organizer, will manage the site, which 
will be hosted at the Universiti Pertanian Malaysia-Malaysian
Technology Development Corporation (UPM-MTDC) Incubation Centre, 
located within the vicinity of Malaysia's Multimedia Super Corridor.

     The Malaysian site primarily targets Internet users in Asia and 
will provide them with faster response to their AltaVista Internet 
search queries because their requests for Internet information will 
be serviced in Asia rather than from the U.S.  When complete, the 
mirror site will provide Asian Internet users with searches that 
bring Asian-based Web content to the forefront.  In addition, Alam 
Teknokrat will offer related intranet services to corporate 
customers in the region.  The site is expected to be operational 
by mid-1997.  

     Also today, Alam Teknokrat Sdn Bhd signed a systems integration 
agreement with HTI Systems Sdn Bhd, a Digital Equipment (M) Sdn Bhd 
business partner, for the purpose of implementing the AltaVista 
mirror site.

     Responding to the rapid growth of Internet users from outside 
the United States, AltaVista is aggressively implementing plans to 
mirror the search service by establishing the AltaVista Worldwide 
Network.  The Network will include sites in Europe, Asia, Australia, 
Latin America, and Africa, managed by Affiliate partners in each 
region.  Affiliates use the same index, search and retrieval 
software as the home site in Palo Alto, California 
(http://www.altavista.digital.com), but adapt the service to the 
needs of their users by translating the user interface and help 
pages into local languages and providing content, advertising, and 
related services targeted to their regional markets.  To date, 
AltaVista Internet Software, Inc. has established two mirror sites:  
in Northern Europe (http://www.altavista.telia.com) with Affiliate 
Telia TeleCom AB of Sweden; and in Australia 
(http://www.altavista.yellowpages.com.au) with Affiliate 
Telstra/Yellow Pages. 

     "We are very pleased to partner with Alam Teknokrat for this 
next step in the expansion and growth of the AltaVista Worldwide 
Network," said Ilene H. Lang, president and chief executive officer 
of AltaVista Internet Software, Inc., and vice president of Digital 
Equipment Corporation. "Internet use is growing explosively in Asia, 
and we anticipate great interest in the AltaVista Search service.  
Based in Malaysia's Multimedia Super Corridor, this mirror site will 
provide access to AltaVista for significantly more Asian users at 
higher performance, and will open opportunities for companies 
seeking to use the Internet and intranets for business purposes."

     On the same note, YBhg, Dato Prof. Dr. Muhammad Ridzuan Salleh, 
chairman of Alam Teknokrat Sdn Bhd said, "We are equally pleased and 
honored to have been afforded the opportunity to be an Asian 
affiliate of the AltaVista Worldwide Network. The establishment of 
this Asian mirror site signifies Alam Teknokrat's commitment to 
facilitating and developing the growth and use of the Internet in 
Asia.  Simultaneously, we intend to position ourselves as one of the 
major catalysts in realizing the Government's effort to promote 
Malaysia as a regional hub for the development and growth of the 
Information Technology industry."

     HTI Systems Sdn Bhd's executive director, Kamaluddin Abdullah 
Badawi, in reference to the systems integration component of the 
AltaVista Asian mirror site said, "As a home-grown Malaysian company 
we are especially pleased to play our part in helping other 
Malaysian companies take Malaysia to the forefront of technological 
excellence in the world of the Internet.  Our role here ties in 
neatly with our corporate tag line of Computing for the Future."

     Jamaludin Ibrahim, chief executive officer and managing 
director of Digital Equipment (M) Sdn Bhd said, "Digital Malaysia is 
extremely proud to have Malaysia chosen as the third mirror site in 
the world for the AltaVista Worldwide Network expansion.  It is 
indeed a timely decision in sync with the vast growth of the IT 
industry in the region.  This also goes to show that the world 
recognizes Malaysia for its technological skills and credibility."

     The AltaVista Internet Search service, created by Digital 
Equipment Corporation researchers in Palo Alto, California and 
operated by Digital's AltaVista Internet Software subsidiary, 
enables an Internet user to find precise information on the 
World Wide Web and the Usenet newsgroups without having to know 
where on the Internet the information resides. AltaVista's index 
includes over 15 billion words from more than 30 million Web pages 
on over 275,600 Web servers around the world, plus four million 
articles from 14,000 USENET newsgroups.  It is the fastest and most 
popular search engine on the Internet, responding to more than 24 
million queries daily with sub-second performance.

     AltaVista OnSite Computing solutions provide secure, simple 
and direct access to information and people over the Internet and 
private intranets.  AltaVista Search, Directory, Tunnel, Firewall, 
Forum and Mail products give users a competitive edge, enabling 
productive business to take place from anywhere.  Further 
information on AltaVista OnSite Computing is available at 
http://www.altavista.software.digital.com, or by calling 
1-800-336-7890 in the U.S.

     Alam Teknokrat Sdn Bhd is an entrepreneurial company providing 
a broad range of Internet tools and solutions to allow businesses 
improved interaction with their customers. Alam Teknokrat also 
enhances the online experience of Internet users by providing an 
easy-to-use search platform that is current, entertaining, and 
informative.

     HTI Systems is an IT solutions company specializing in systems 
integration, consultancy services, application services as well as 
operation and maintenance services.  With its corporate tag line 
"Computing for the Future," its breadth of commercial and industrial 
solutions, and the depth of its technology applications, HTI Systems 
aims to be a premier IT solutions provider contributing 
significantly to the development of the Multimedia Super Corridor.

